  "live_records": {
    "q-160767": {
      "dom_id": "step-q160767",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
