    "q-162650": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162650",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t))\\,i+3t\\,j+(2-{t}^{2})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $2-{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
