    "q-162662": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162662",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t}$ is $t\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)$ is $s\\in (-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{t}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117176/assets/971a65619088884002784f5abb3c4f3dc9b2e17e6b905f171b8106219a139557.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
