    "q-162663": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162663",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=\\sqrt{1-s}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-s)\\,k.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{1-s}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,1].$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,0).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117176/assets/6a2d170c22a544335735e859dd080d74964a4d5b5053789a557b5ea406f9d3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (-2,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
